band that you might want to check out. It's New Order.

01:55:50.810 --> 01:55:52.480
Formed in Manchester, England in 19...

01:55:53.150 --> 01:55:55.350
Three remaining members of the post-point joy division.

01:55:55.580 --> 01:55:58.160
Bernard Sumner, Peter Hook, and Stephen Morris

01:55:58.160 --> 01:55:59.640
following the suicide death...

01:56:00.000 --> 01:56:03.940
singer ian curtis with the addition of morris's girlfriend gillian gilbert on synthesizer new

01:56:03.940 --> 01:56:08.540
order went on to earn both commercial and critical success with their blend of new wave pop and catchy

01:56:08.540 --> 01:56:12.370
techno dance music the band's sound was a little brighter than joy division's but it was still

01:56:12.370 --> 01:56:16.990
quite moody now sumner took over on lead vocals and his monotone and emotionally remote voice

01:56:16.990 --> 01:56:22.240
became the center of that group's sound the band's first album 1981's movement wisely downplayed

01:56:22.240 --> 01:56:26.590
the vocals for which joy division was so well known and instead concentrated on developing

01:56:26.590 --> 01:56:29.970
electronic sounds. The album featured both great guitars and synthesizers.

01:56:30.570 --> 01:56:35.920
songs like dreams never end after the release the 1981 82 ep which consisted of five songs

01:56:35.920 --> 01:56:39.960
taken from british singles including everything's gone green and the classic temptation the band

01:56:39.960 --> 01:56:44.780
scored a breakthrough in 83 with a huge uk dance hit blue monday which was only released as a 12

01:56:44.780 --> 01:56:49.220
inch single but ended up selling three million copies worldwide ben once told me that they never

01:56:49.220 --> 01:56:53.580
made any money off that 12 inch because of the fact that packaging was so nice and so expensive

01:56:53.580 --> 01:56:58.730
they followed up this one with a release of their second album 1983's power corruption and lies

01:56:58.730 --> 01:56:59.960
is considered by some to be

01:57:00.090 --> 01:57:03.750
masterpiece. It's emotionally intense and it blends electronic dance music with

01:57:03.750 --> 01:57:07.970
moody lyrics. Includes classics like Age of Consent and Leave Me Alone. In 85,

01:57:08.570 --> 01:57:11.970
Noorder left their label Factory Records and signed with Quincy Jones' Quest

01:57:11.970 --> 01:57:15.390
label. That same year they released Low Life, which was their introduction to

01:57:15.390 --> 01:57:19.270
America basically, with great songs like Perfect Kiss, Love Vigilantes, Face Up,

01:57:19.410 --> 01:57:22.530
Subculture. The band successfully explored new musical territory without

01:57:22.530 --> 01:57:27.020
abandoning their basic format. Their next album was 86's Brotherhood, featured the

01:57:27.020 --> 01:57:28.980
huge hit, Bizarre Love Triangle. You heard that

01:57:28.980 --> 01:57:29.880
in clubs all over.

01:57:30.640 --> 01:57:35.600
Anyway, the following year, they released a career retrospective double album called Substance in 1987,

01:57:35.620 --> 01:57:41.720
which include all of their classic hits, from Ceremony to Thieves Like Us, you know, State of the Nation.

01:57:42.100 --> 01:57:45.870
Now in 89, the band released the album Technique, which included the hit True Faith,

01:57:46.050 --> 01:57:48.630
which was a breakthrough here in America, even a Top 40 hit.

01:57:48.900 --> 01:57:50.680
But the members weren't that crazy about their fame.

01:57:51.080 --> 01:57:54.320
Shortly thereafter, they decided to go their separate ways in order to explore solo projects.

01:57:54.730 --> 01:57:58.390
Now Bernie Sumner joined up with ex-Smith's guitarist, Johnny Marr, to form Electronic,

01:57:58.390 --> 01:57:59.880
while bass's hook featured

01:58:00.250 --> 01:58:05.010
side project called Revenge and in 97 formed another band called Monaco with David Potts and

01:58:05.010 --> 01:58:09.740
both sounded a lot like New Order. Now Morrison Gilbert released an album under the moniker of

01:58:09.770 --> 01:58:15.360
The Other Two. The band reformed in 93 to release Republic followed by a successful tour of the U.S.

01:58:15.460 --> 01:58:20.220
and their final release was a 1995 anthology which picks up where Substance left off titled

01:58:20.220 --> 01:58:24.490
The Best New Order. Both of those last two albums feature the great song Regret. Now the band is

01:58:24.490 --> 01:58:28.670
supposed to reunite for the first time in nearly five years to play some dates this summer including

01:58:28.720 --> 01:58:29.960
the Reading Festival in England.

